From: K230 AMP development <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: k230: describe small-core AMP slot on CanMV-K230 LCD

k230-canmv-lcd.dts includes k230.dtsi directly rather than k230-canmv.dts, so
it does not inherit the AMP carveout or the UART3 handover.

k230_canmv_small_core_defconfig lists the non-LCD DTS first, so this DTB is not
the one booted and the omission is currently harmless. It is still a trap:
booting k230-canmv-lcd.dtb in the AMP configuration would let Linux allocate
straight into the big core's firmware and shared-memory windows. Describe the
reservation here too so either DTB is safe.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-lcd.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-lcd.dts
@@ -25,6 +25,22 @@
 		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x20000000>;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		big_core_firmware: big-core-firmware@1c000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1c000000 0x0 0x01000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		amp_shared_memory: amp-shared-memory@1d000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1d000000 0x0 0x03000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sound {
 		status                      = "okay";
 		compatible                  = "canaan,k230-audio-inno";
@@ -37,8 +53,9 @@
 &uart0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+/* UART3 is connected to CH342 channel B and belongs to big-core firmware. */
 &uart3 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 &mmc_sd1{
 	status = "okay";
